# what: what the build context must NOT carry into the image.
# why:  two reasons, and the second one is the serious one. A slimmer context
#       builds faster -- but more importantly, `.env` holds credentials, and a
#       file copied into an image is in that image forever, readable by anyone
#       who can pull it. Secrets reach a container through the ENVIRONMENT at
#       run time, never through a COPY.
# how:  the Dockerfile copies only requirements.txt, agent/ and runbooks/, so
#       most of this is belt and braces. It is written out anyway because the
#       next person to add a COPY line will not re-derive the reasoning.

.env
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.db
.git/
.gitignore
.pytest_cache/
audit.jsonl
code.bash
output.bash
CLAUDE.md
mvp_plan.md
*.md
!runbooks/*.md

# Stage 5 run state: the audit trail and the demo trails.
audit.jsonl
demo_*.jsonl
